DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ssttrrccoollll() function lexicographically compares the null-terminated
     strings _s_1 and _s_2 according to the current locale collation and returns
     an integer greater than, equal to, or less than 0, depending on whether
     _s_1 is greater than, equal to, or less than _s_2.  If information about the
     current locale collation is not available, the value of ssttrrccmmpp(_s_1, _s_2) is
     returned.  The ssttrrccoollll__ll() function uses an explicit locale argument
     rather than the system locale.

